# GitHub Issues and PRs

Read `AGENTS.md` §13 **GitHub Issue Structure** and **Feature branch rule** for the full rules.

## Feature branch (before any commit)

- Each new spec MUST have branch `NNN-feature-slug` (e.g. `002-mcp-transport-adapter`) **before the first commit** for that spec
- Spec kit artifacts, fixtures, tasks, and implementation all go on that branch — **never on `main`**
- Confirm `git branch --show-current` is the feature branch before committing; merge to `main` via PR only

## When creating issues (`/speckit-taskstoissues`)

- One **epic** per spec; one **sub-issue** per phase/user story in `tasks.md`
- Tasks (`T001`, …) are checkboxes inside sub-issue bodies — never standalone issues
- Write `specs/<feature>/github-issues.md` with all issue numbers and a **PR issue references** block

## When creating an implementation PR

1. Read `specs/<feature>/github-issues.md`
2. Include an **Issues resolved** section with `Refs #NNN` for the epic **and every sub-issue**
3. Use `.github/pull_request_template.md` as the starting structure

Epic and sub-issues follow the same lifecycle: `under-review` → `pending-release` → `released`. Do not use `Closes #NNN` — release automation closes issues when a GitHub release is published.
